============================================================================================
(i) k=9 tent (a = 5/63): random+descent search for min ring sum vs theory 1 - 9a = 18/63
============================================================================================
    search min = 0.285714; theory m = 1 - 9*(5/63) = 0.285714 = 2/7
    floor = 1 - 72*((1/7 - 5/63)^2/2)/(2/7) = 0.492063 = 31/63 = 0.492063

(ii) ring-2 on the binding face: all gaps >= 5/63 => 2-sums >= 10/63 > 9/63 = 1/7: True

============================================================================================
(iii) conditional-tent arithmetic (c = discrepancy factor, program target c <= 1.7)
============================================================================================
    k=9, c=1.0: rho* >= meas(G_P)*(1 - c*(1-floor)) = 0.2432 >= m_P 0.0565: True
    k=9, c=1.3: rho* >= meas(G_P)*(1 - c*(1-floor)) = 0.1679 >= m_P 0.0565: True
    k=9, c=1.7: rho* >= meas(G_P)*(1 - c*(1-floor)) = 0.0675 >= m_P 0.0565: True
    k=10, c=1.0: rho* >= meas(G_P)*(1 - c*(1-floor)) = 0.1381 >= m_P 0.0565: True
    k=10, c=1.3: rho* >= meas(G_P)*(1 - c*(1-floor)) = -0.0017 >= m_P 0.0565: False
    k=10, c=1.7: rho* >= meas(G_P)*(1 - c*(1-floor)) = -0.1882 >= m_P 0.0565: False

    => at c = 1 (no discrepancy): k=9 headroom 4.3x, k=10 headroom 2.4x;
       c <= 1.7 suffices at k=9; c <= 1.3-ish at k=10.  The finite program:
       exact int_{G_P} f(frac(dx)) tables for small d per P + Koksma tail for large d.
